IMPORT policy

-- Standing preamble, applied to every question below: assume all
-- conditions unrelated to that question are met, and no exclusions
-- unrelated to it apply. Concretely, unless a question's own facts say
-- otherwise:
--   * there is no fraud or misrepresentation;
--   * the wellness visit itself is treated as having happened comfortably
--     on time (month 1), since none of the nine questions give a separate
--     fact about when the visit itself -- as opposed to the written
--     confirmation of it -- took place;
--   * the written confirmation of the wellness visit is treated as having
--     been supplied on time (month 1) whenever a question does not mention
--     it at all;
--   * the hospitalization month defaults to 1 (comfortably inside the
--     one-year term) whenever a question does not give it a number.
-- Also assumed, per the task's own preamble: the agreement has been signed
-- and the premium paid on time.

-- Q1: hospitalized by burns suffered while on duty as a firefighter.
-- The cause is squarely "service as a fire fighter" (Section 2.1, item 3).
q1 MEANS Claim WITH
    `cause of hospitalization`    IS `Firefighter Service`
    `age at hospitalization`      IS 40
    `hospitalization month`       IS 1
    `wellness visit month`        IS JUST 1
    `wellness confirmation month` IS JUST 1
    `fraud or misrepresentation`  IS FALSE
#EVAL `covered` q1

-- Q2: 78 years old at the time of hospitalization -- below the age-80
-- exclusion threshold in Section 2.1, item 5.
q2 MEANS Claim WITH
    `cause of hospitalization`    IS Other
    `age at hospitalization`      IS 78
    `hospitalization month`       IS 1
    `wellness visit month`        IS JUST 1
    `wellness confirmation month` IS JUST 1
    `fraud or misrepresentation`  IS FALSE
#EVAL `covered` q2

-- Q3: hospitalized for pneumonia 5 months after the effective date, age 65.
-- Pneumonia is not an excluded cause, age is below 80, and 5 months is
-- comfortably before either wellness-condition deadline.
q3 MEANS Claim WITH
    `cause of hospitalization`    IS Other
    `age at hospitalization`      IS 65
    `hospitalization month`       IS 5
    `wellness visit month`        IS JUST 1
    `wellness confirmation month` IS JUST 1
    `fraud or misrepresentation`  IS FALSE
#EVAL `covered` q3

-- Q4: hospitalized after a fall while traveling abroad; confirmation of
-- the wellness visit was given 8 months after the effective date -- after
-- the Section 1.3 / 7-month deadline, so the condition was violated and
-- the policy stands canceled under Section 1.2. A fall is not an excluded
-- cause, and Section 3.1.1 covers the insured worldwide, so "abroad" does
-- not matter.
q4 MEANS Claim WITH
    `cause of hospitalization`    IS Other
    `age at hospitalization`      IS 40
    `hospitalization month`       IS 1
    `wellness visit month`        IS JUST 1
    `wellness confirmation month` IS JUST 8
    `fraud or misrepresentation`  IS FALSE
#EVAL `covered` q4

-- Q5: hospitalized for punching his own face to show off for friends, with
-- no fraud or misrepresentation. Self-inflicted horseplay is not on the
-- Section 2.1 exclusion list, so nothing excludes it.
q5 MEANS Claim WITH
    `cause of hospitalization`    IS Other
    `age at hospitalization`      IS 40
    `hospitalization month`       IS 1
    `wellness visit month`        IS JUST 1
    `wellness confirmation month` IS JUST 1
    `fraud or misrepresentation`  IS FALSE
#EVAL `covered` q5

-- Q6: injured while skydiving, age 79, wellness-visit proof provided 6.5
-- months after the effective date. Skydiving is excluded outright
-- (Section 2.1, item 1) regardless of the age or the wellness timing.
q6 MEANS Claim WITH
    `cause of hospitalization`    IS Skydiving
    `age at hospitalization`      IS 79
    `hospitalization month`       IS 1
    `wellness visit month`        IS JUST 1
    `wellness confirmation month` IS JUST 6.5
    `fraud or misrepresentation`  IS FALSE
#EVAL `covered` q6

-- Q7: hospitalized for a heart attack, wellness-visit proof submitted 2
-- months after the effective date, age 75. Not an excluded cause, age
-- below 80, and well within both wellness-condition deadlines.
q7 MEANS Claim WITH
    `cause of hospitalization`    IS Other
    `age at hospitalization`      IS 75
    `hospitalization month`       IS 1
    `wellness visit month`        IS JUST 1
    `wellness confirmation month` IS JUST 2
    `fraud or misrepresentation`  IS FALSE
#EVAL `covered` q7

-- Q8: injured in a military training exercise, hospitalization within the
-- policy term, no fraud. A training exercise performed as part of
-- military service is "service in the military" (Section 2.1, item 2).
q8 MEANS Claim WITH
    `cause of hospitalization`    IS `Military Service`
    `age at hospitalization`      IS 40
    `hospitalization month`       IS 1
    `wellness visit month`        IS JUST 1
    `wellness confirmation month` IS JUST 1
    `fraud or misrepresentation`  IS FALSE
#EVAL `covered` q8

-- Q9: hospitalized because the claimant's son bit his ankle; wellness-visit
-- proof provided 6 months after the effective date; the claimant was
-- serving as a police officer at the time. The cause of the injury is the
-- bite, not the claimant's police service -- being a police officer does
-- not itself trigger Section 2.1, item 4, because the injury did not arise
-- out of that service.
q9 MEANS Claim WITH
    `cause of hospitalization`    IS Other
    `age at hospitalization`      IS 40
    `hospitalization month`       IS 1
    `wellness visit month`        IS JUST 1
    `wellness confirmation month` IS JUST 6
    `fraud or misrepresentation`  IS FALSE
#EVAL `covered` q9
